The aarch64 virt board gets virtio-vga, as the x86, PPC and RISC-V
boards have it: virtio-gpu with QEMU's VGA core, whose linear frame
buffer the firmware's QemuVideoDxe drives and Windows' Basic Display
inherits, while the virtio half is the guest driver's. 2ksbox's
Windows 11 on Arm machines then have one screen, with no ramfb beside
the virtio-gpu for the firmware and setup.
Drop when upstream's virt board implies VIRTIO_VGA.

diff --git a/hw/arm/Kconfig b/hw/arm/Kconfig
index 6f5b2ad..9c7a13d 100644
--- a/hw/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/arm/Kconfig
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ config ARM_VIRT
     depends on ARM
     depends on TCG || KVM || HVF
     imply PCI_DEVICES
+    imply VIRTIO_VGA
     imply TEST_DEVICES
     imply TPM_TIS_SYSBUS
     imply TPM_TIS_I2C
